<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"><title><%= title %> - EliteHackLab</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/css/all.min.css"></head>
<body>
  <div class="matrix-bg"></div>
  <nav class="main-nav"><div class="nav-brand"><span class="brand-icon">💀</span><span class="brand-text">Elite<span class="highlight">Hack</span>Lab</span></div><div class="nav-links"><a href="/"><i class="fas fa-home"></i> Dashboard</a></div></nav>
  <div class="lab-container">
    <div class="lab-header"><h1><i class="fas fa-plug"></i> API Security Labs</h1></div>
    <div class="lab-section"><h2><i class="fas fa-book"></i> Theory</h2><p>API security vulnerabilities are among the most common attack vectors in modern applications. These labs cover mass assignment, rate limiting bypass, GraphQL introspection, NoSQL injection, and API key exposure in real-world scenarios.</p></div>
    <div class="lab-section"><h2><i class="fas fa-flask"></i> Labs</h2><div class="lab-list"><% labs.forEach(function(lab) { %><a href="<%= lab.path %>" class="lab-link"><span class="lab-name"><i class="fas fa-terminal"></i> <%= lab.name %></span><span class="lab-difficulty <%= lab.difficulty.toLowerCase().split('-')[0] %>"><%= lab.difficulty %></span></a><% }); %></div></div>
  </div>
  <script src="/js/main.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
